# Cloudflare Workers Assets serves everything with
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
# by default, so a repeat visitor makes a conditional request for every single
# file — CSS, JS, the logo, all six Lottie JSONs — just to be told 304. That is
# a round trip per asset on every page view.
#
# 7 days, not a year: xtract.css/js carry a ?v=N cache-buster so they could be
# immutable, but the images and Lottie JSON do not, and a year of immutable on
# an unversioned file means a replaced image never reaches anyone. A week kills
# the revalidation traffic while keeping a sane worst case; stale-while-
# revalidate lets the refresh happen in the background.
#
# HTML is deliberately left alone — it must keep revalidating so content and
# version bumps appear immediately.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Security headers on every response. This is a static marketing site with no
# accounts, payments or user input, so the real risk these close is low — the
# reason they are here is that a prospective client sizing up a web agency may
# run the domain through securityheaders.io, and an unset site scores an F.
#
# HSTS is the one with genuine value: it tells the browser never to use plain
# HTTP for this domain again, closing the one unencrypted request that happens
# when someone types the bare hostname and gets the http->https 301. One year,
# includeSubDomains. Not adding `preload` — that is a hard commitment to HTTPS
# on every subdomain forever and is deliberately left off.
#
# The rest are cheap hardening: nosniff stops content-type guessing, the frame
# and referrer rules are clickjacking and privacy hygiene. No CSP: a correct
# one would have to enumerate the Google Fonts, the cdn.hephoratech.com widget
# and every inline script, and a wrong one silently breaks the page — not worth
# it here.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
